treeweave
Copyright 2025-2026 Marco Barbone and the treeweave authors.

treeweave is an independent reimplementation inspired by baobzi
(https://github.com/flatironinstitute/baobzi), an "adaptive fast function
approximator based on tree search" by Robert Blackwell and the Flatiron
Institute.

baobzi originated the adaptive-tree-of-polynomial-panels design that treeweave
builds on. treeweave shares no code with baobzi: it is a clean reimplementation
that re-architects the fit and evaluation pipeline around polyfit
(https://github.com/DiamonDinoia/polyfit) and POET
(https://github.com/DiamonDinoia/poet) and adds a multi-language C ABI.

